t] operation The key derivation operation object to read from.\0A * \5Cparam[out] key          On success, an identifier for the newly created\0A *                          key. For persistent keys, this is the key\0A *                          identifier defined in \5Cp attributes.\0A *                          \5Cc 0 on failure.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A *         If the key is persistent, the key material and the key's metadata\0A *         have been saved to persistent storage.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS\0A *         This is an attempt to create a persistent key, and there is\0A *         already a persistent key with the given identifier.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_DATA\0A *         There was not enough data to create the desired key.\0A *         Note that in this case, no output is written to the output buffer.\0A *         The operation's capacity is set to 0, thus subsequent calls to\0A *         this function will not succeed, even with a smaller output buffer.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         The key type or key size is not supported, either by the\0A *         implementation in general or in this particular location.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         The provided key attributes are not valid for the operation.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_PERMITTED\0A *         The #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET or\0A *         #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_PASSWORD input was not provided through a\0A *         key; or one of the inputs was a key whose policy didn't allow\0A *         #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_HARDWARE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_INVALID \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_CORRUPT \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be active and completed\0A *         all required input steps), or the library has not been previously\0A *         initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_key_derivation_output_key(\0A    const psa_key_attributes_t *attributes,\0A    psa_key_derivation_operation_t *operation,\0A    mbedtls_svc_key_id_t *key);\0A\0A/** Derive a key from an ongoing key derivation operation with custom\0A *  production parameters.\0A *\0A * See the description of psa_key_derivation_out_key() for the operation of\0A * this function with the default production parameters.\0A * Mbed TLS currently does not currently support any non-default production\0A * parameters.\0A *\0A * \5Cnote This function is experimental and may change in future minor\0A *       versions of Mbed TLS.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in] attributes    The attributes for the new key.\0A *                          If the key type to be created is\0A *                          #PSA_KEY_TYPE_PASSWORD_HASH then the algorithm in\0A *                          the policy must be the same as in the current\0A *                          operation.\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation The key derivation operation object to read from.\0A * \5Cparam[in] custom        Customization parameters for the key generation.\0A *                          When this is #PSA_CUSTOM_KEY_PARAMETERS_INIT\0A *                          with \5Cp custom_data_length = 0,\0A *                          this function is equivalent to\0A *                          psa_key_derivation_output_key().\0A * \5Cparam[in] custom_data   Variable-length data associated with \5Cc custom.\0A * \5Cparam custom_data_length\0A *                          Length of `custom_data` in bytes.\0A * \5Cparam[out] key          On success, an identifier for the newly created\0A *                          key. For persistent keys, this is the key\0A *                          identifier defined in \5Cp attributes.\0A *                          \5Cc 0 on failure.\0A *\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_SUCCESS\0A *         Success.\0A *         If the key is persistent, the key material and the key's metadata\0A *         have been saved to persistent storage.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_ALREADY_EXISTS\0A *         This is an attempt to create a persistent key, and there is\0A *         already a persistent key with the given identifier.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_DATA\0A *         There was not enough data to create the desired key.\0A *         Note that in this case, no output is written to the output buffer.\0A *         The operation's capacity is set to 0, thus subsequent calls to\0A *         this function will not succeed, even with a smaller output buffer.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED\0A *         The key type or key size is not supported, either by the\0A *         implementation in general or in this particular location.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\0A *         The provided key attributes are not valid for the operation.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_NOT_PERMITTED\0A *         The #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_SECRET or\0A *         #PSA_KEY_DERIVATION_INPUT_PASSWORD input was not provided through a\0A *         key; or one of the inputs was a key whose policy didn't allow\0A *         #PSA_KEY_USAGE_DERIVE.\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_STORAGE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_COMMUNICATION_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_HARDWARE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_CORRUPTION_DETECTED \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_INVALID \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_DATA_CORRUPT \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_STORAGE_FAILURE \5Cemptydescription\0A * \5Cretval #PSA_ERROR_BAD_STATE\0A *         The operation state is not valid (it must be active and completed\0A *         all required input steps), or the library has not been previously\0A *         initialized by psa_crypto_init().\0A *         It is implementation-dependent whether a failure to initialize\0A *         results in this error code.\0A */\0Apsa_status_t psa_key_derivation_output_key_custom(\0A    const psa_key_attributes_t *attributes,\0A    psa_key_derivation_operation_t *operation,\0A    const psa_custom_key_parameters_t *custom,\0A    const uint8_t *custom_data,\0A    size_t custom_data_length,\0A    mbedtls_svc_key_id_t *key);\0A\0A#ifndef __cplusplus\0A/* Omitted when compiling in C++, because one of the parameters is a\0A * pointer to a struct with a flexible array member, and that is not\0A * standard C++.\0A * https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls/issues/9020\0A */\0A/** Derive a key from an ongoing key derivation operation with custom\0A *  production parameters.\0A *\0A * \5Cnote\0A * This is a deprecated variant of psa_key_derivation_output_key_custom().\0A * It is equivalent except that the associated variable-length data\0A * is passed in `params->data` instead of a separate parameter.\0A * This function will be removed in a future version of Mbed TLS.\0A *\0A * \5Cparam[in] attributes    The attributes for the new key.\0A *                          If the key type to be created is\0A *                          #PSA_KEY_TYPE_PASSWORD_HASH then the algorithm in\0A *                          the policy must be the same as in the current\0A *                          operation.\0A * \5Cparam[in,out] operation The key derivation operation object to read from.\0A * \5Cparam[in] params        Customization parameters for the key derivation.\0A *                          When this is #PSA_KEY_PRODUCTION_P